[LSIG.2.3.2] On a new assertion $(t_{\mathrm{new}}, x_{\mathrm{new}})$ the
runtime, in this order:

1. closes the open interval: $S \leftarrow S + x_{\mathrm{open}}\,(t_{\mathrm{new}} - t_{\mathrm{open}})$;
2. evicts the expired entries from the ring and subtracts their contribution
   from $S$, clipping a partial interval at the window boundary;
3. pushes $(t_{\mathrm{open}}, x_{\mathrm{open}})$, the just-closed interval's
   **start**, as [LSIG.2.3.1] stores entries and [LSIG.2.3.3] reads them;
4. sets $x_{\mathrm{open}} = x_{\mathrm{new}}$ and $t_{\mathrm{open}} = t_{\mathrm{new}}$.
